WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.743
PostgreSQL can subtract one timestamp from another
The result

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:11.410
is an INTERVAL representing elapsed time This is the
direct way to answer

00:00:11.436 --> 00:00:17.037
questions such as length of stay or processing
duration If you later need

00:00:17.063 --> 00:00:20.945
a numeric number of hours or days that is a separate
conversion step
